{
  "id": "battle-roads",
  "name": "Battle Roads (Play! Pokémon)",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "Battle Roads were Play! Pokémon's local tournaments outside Japan, named after Japan's Battle Road but much smaller: independent organizers ran them in game and hobby stores across North America, as a step up from weekly League play where players could raise their rating, and from 2011 earn Championship Points, toward the World Championships. A season ran from one World Championships to the next, with an autumn circuit in September and October and a spring one in May and June; the first season had only a spring circuit, played in 2007.\n\nUntil spring 2011 the winner of each tournament got a Victory Medal card stamped with its season, a gold medal in spring and a silver one in autumn. The medals beside Pikachu reuse the art of the Victory Medals won at Japan's Official Pokémon Card Gym events, and the 2010-2011 medals show Typhlosion and a Play! Pokémon logo. From autumn 2011 the top three each got a Victory Cup card stamped with the season, art first given at Japan's 2011 Battle Carnival. Battle Road Spring 2013 was the last tournament of the name anywhere.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Pokumon: US Battle Road Events",
        "url": "https://pokumon.com/us-battle-road-events/"
      },
